       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 2,000 mg dose is also double the typical 1,000 mg maximum. At this dose there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
